From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] drm/exynos7580: document CMA sizing + COHERENCY_NONE

Record the two board facts a GEM author must not re-derive:

- CMA: shipping defconfig has CONFIG_CMA_SIZE_MBYTES=0 (no default
  CMA area; __dma_alloc_coherent falls through to swiotlb), so real
  GEM/dumb allocations need the 32 MB raised by the display config
  fragment (covers 720x1280x4 double scanout ~7.4 MB + GEM slack;
  revisit 64 MB only on measured CMA pressure at the M2 import
  path). No DT reserved-memory/linux,cma node exists, so the Kconfig
  knob is the only sizing control (cma= cmdline can still override).

- Coherency: the SoC is non-coherent as far as the GPU is concerned
  (mali_kbase_core_linux.c:3577 forces COHERENCY_NONE; mali@0x11400000
  has no system-coherency property). Consequences already handled by
  the code a panfrost port must mirror: explicit page-table
  maintenance (kbase_mmu_sync_pgd), DMA-sync discipline on UMM
  sharing, WC (not cached) CPU mapping for scanout. AS_MEMATTR
  kbase-vs-panfrost divergence (0x8D884D4F48 vs 0x888D88) stays a
  correctness item (R4).

Comment-only; no code change.

---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/exynos7580/exynos7580_drm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/exynos7580/exynos7580_drm.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/exynos7580/exynos7580_drm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/exynos7580/exynos7580_drm.c
@@ -537,5 +537,27 @@ static const struct dev_pm_ops exynos7580_pm_ops = {
 };
 
 /* ---------------------------------------------------------------------- */
+/*
+ * CMA sizing (this board): the shipping defconfig sets
+ * CONFIG_CMA_SIZE_MBYTES=0, i.e. no default CMA area, so GEM/dumb
+ * allocations need the 32 MB from the display config fragment
+ * (covers 720x1280x4 double-buffered scanout plus GEM slack).
+ * There is no DT reserved-memory/linux,cma node: the Kconfig knob
+ * (still overridable via the cma= cmdline) is the only control.
+ * Revisit 64 MB only on measured CMA pressure at the M2 import path.
+ *
+ * Coherency (this SoC): COHERENCY_NONE. kbase forces it at
+ * mali_kbase_core_linux.c:3577 (no system-coherency property on
+ * mali@0x11400000), so a panfrost-class GEM/MMU must use
+ * coherent_walk = false + explicit dma_sync after every page-table
+ * update (cf. kbase_mmu_sync_pgd), and WC (Normal Non-Cached) CPU
+ * mappings for scanout need no cache flush. The AS_MEMATTR
+ * kbase-vs-upstream divergence (0x8D884D4F48 vs 0x888D88) remains
+ * correctness item R4: keep the kbase table on this silicon until a
+ * GPU-read test says otherwise.
+ *
+ * The GPU programs its own MMU (AS_TRANSTAB/MEMATTR/COMMAND); no
+ * sysmmu/exynos-iommu involvement exists on the GPU path.
+ */
 /* GEM/IOMMU helpers							  */
 /* ---------------------------------------------------------------------- */
